## P2-D3: Create VFS-Aware Product Query Functions

### Scope Contract
Build data layer functions that use VFS keys for product discovery. Replace legacy categoryPath matching.

**Files Created:**
- `sanity/lib/products/getProductsByVfsKeys.ts` — VFS-enabled product query
- `sanity/lib/products/getFeaturedProductsByVfsKeys.ts` — featured products by category

**Files Modified:**
- `sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts` — add VFS key path support

### DoD — Data Layer Implementation

-- [ ] 3.1 — Create `getProductsByVfsKeys.ts` with function `getProductsByVfsKeys(vfsKeys: string[], limit?: number)`. GROQ query: `*[_type == "product" && count(catalogueLocationKeys[@ in $vfsKeys]) > 0] | order(name asc)`. Returns products array.
  - Difficulty: 4 - A(sanity/lib/products/getProductsByVfsKeys.ts): create VFS product query

-- [ ] 3.2 — Create `getFeaturedProductsByVfsKeys.ts` with function `getFeaturedProductsByVfsKeys(vfsKeys: string[], featuredCount: number)`. Extends base query with featured flag or manual selection.
  - Difficulty: 3 - A(sanity/lib/products/getFeaturedProductsByVfsKeys.ts): create featured VFS query

-- [ ] 3.3 — Update `getSelectedProducts.ts` to accept `catalogueKeys: string[]` and use VFS query pattern `count(catalogueLocationKeys[@ in $catalogueKeys]) > 0`. Remove legacy categoryPath matching code.
  - Difficulty: 5 - C(sanity/lib/products/getSelectedProducts.ts): migrate to VFS key queries

-- [ ] 3.4 — Test `getProductsByVfsKeys` with real slug "open-back": resolve to ID, unroll keys, fetch products. Verify returned products have matching catalogueLocationKeys.
  - Difficulty: 3 - D(sanity/lib/products): manual test VFS query

### Verification — P2-D3

-- [ ] V3.1 — Test query: `getProductsByVfsKeys(["o7c6baiuobsr7ni2y2vf22sh"])` returns only open-back headphones.
  - Difficulty: 2

-- [ ] V3.2 — Test query: `getProductsByVfsKeys(unrollDescendantKeys("ugyeto8653n495dpf89nzoar"))` returns all headphone products (open-back, closed-back, planar, etc.).
  - Difficulty: 2

